mac80211_hwsim: make the simulated custom regdom authoritative for 6 GHz

OPTIONAL, independent of the multichannel change in 0001. Needed only if the lab
brings up 6 GHz (band 3) APs.

Two tweaks so a simulated 6 GHz AP is allowed to beacon:
  1. Add REGULATORY_STRICT_REG alongside REGULATORY_CUSTOM_REG so the custom
     hwsim regdom is authoritative and is not intersected away by the global
     regulatory domain (which would otherwise mark 6 GHz NO-IR / no-beacon).
  2. Point HWSIM_REGTEST_CUSTOM_WORLD at a 6 GHz-capable custom regdom
     (hwsim_world_regdom_custom_03) instead of _custom_01.

Skip this patch for a 2.4/5 GHz-only lab.

--- a/drivers/net/wireless/virtual/mac80211_hwsim.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/virtual/mac80211_hwsim.c
@@ -5310,6 +5310,7 @@
 	if (param->regd) {
 		data->regd = param->regd;
 		hw->wiphy->regulatory_flags |= REGULATORY_CUSTOM_REG;
+		hw->wiphy->regulatory_flags |= REGULATORY_STRICT_REG;   /* sim: custom regd authoritative, ignore global intersect (6GHz AP) */
 		wiphy_apply_custom_regulatory(hw->wiphy, param->regd);
 		/* give the regulatory workqueue a chance to run */
 		schedule_timeout_interruptible(1);
@@ -6633,7 +6634,7 @@
 				param.regd = &hwsim_world_regdom_custom_01;
 			break;
 		case HWSIM_REGTEST_CUSTOM_WORLD:
-			param.regd = &hwsim_world_regdom_custom_01;
+			param.regd = &hwsim_world_regdom_custom_03;   /* 6GHz-capable regdom */
 			break;
 		case HWSIM_REGTEST_CUSTOM_WORLD_2:
 			if (i == 0)
